WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.670
- [Instructor] We are asked to estimate

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:06.670
what is 2.7 times 4 roughly equal to?

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.130
Pause this video and see
if you can answer that.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.890
Alright, so we can think of 2.7 times 4

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.300
as being roughly equal to,

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.650
or some people might say,

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.528
as approximately equal to.

00:00:20.528 --> 00:00:24.290
Well let's see, 2.7, that's two ones

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.550
and seven tenths.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.232
So we could think about

00:00:27.232 --> 00:00:29.190
well what's the nearest
whole number to 2.7?

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.080
And so 2.7 is pretty close to 3,

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.947
it's in fact closer to 3 than it is to 2.

00:00:33.947 --> 00:00:35.990
So we could say that this is roughly

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.730
equal to three times four.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.577
And then three times four is, of course,

00:00:40.577 --> 00:00:43.290
equal to 12.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.300
And you can see that these other answers

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.598
actually seem quite unreasonable.

00:00:46.598 --> 00:00:49.380
1.2, if I take something

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.810
and I multiply times four,

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.170
I shouldn't get an answer that is

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.960
less than my original something.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.330
And then to go from,

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.350
and then to take something that's

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.370
roughly equal to three times four

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.714
to get to 120, that doesn't make sense,

00:00:59.714 --> 00:01:02.225
and definitely doesn't
make sense to get to 1,200.

00:01:02.225 --> 00:01:04.470
Let's do another example.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.440
So here we said what is roughly

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.840
equal to 78 times 19.88.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.640
So pause this video
and try to answer that.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.820
Alright, well this is
really the same idea.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.040
We wanna think about,

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.740
well what are numbers that
these numbers are close to

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.369
that are easy to multiply with.

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:28.730
So for example, 78, that
is pretty close to 80

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:33.651
and then 19.88, or 19 and 88 hundredths,

00:01:33.651 --> 00:01:36.070
that's pretty close to 20.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.930
It's closer to 20 than it is to 19

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.370
and even if it was closer to 19,

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.763
just to estimate I probably
would still go to 20

00:01:40.763 --> 00:01:44.030
because it's easier to multiply with 20.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.090
So this is going to be pretty close to 20.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.300
So all of this is going to be roughly

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.790
equal to 80 times 20.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:53.460
And you might already recognize

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:58.460
that this is going to be 8
times 2 times 10 times 10

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.360
and I could write it that way,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.100
no reason for me to skip steps.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.950
But you would normally
do this in your head.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.951
So 80 is the same thing as 8 times 10,

00:02:05.951 --> 00:02:07.980
we do that in that purple color

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.270
so that you can see it.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.570
So this is the same thing as 8 times 10

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:17.570
times two times ten
which we could then write

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:23.470
this is going to be 8 times 2 which is 16,

00:02:24.274 --> 00:02:28.900
so the 8 and the 2, you
get 16 times 10 times 10

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.034
is times 100 so this should be 1,600.

00:02:33.034 --> 00:02:37.720
1,600 which is this
choice right over here.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.020
And it's always good to
just do reality check

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.363
to make sure it's reasonable.

00:02:41.363 --> 00:02:43.120
It wouldn't make any sense if I

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.780
take a number close to 80

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.970
and I multiply it by some
number that's close to 20

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.129
and get a smaller number than 80.

00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:52.590
It also, if you have a
number that's close to 80,

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:53.633
to get 160 you'd only have to multiply

00:02:53.633 --> 00:02:55.610
it by roughly 2.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.510
But here we're multiplying by roughly 20.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:02.510
And then to go to 80, or
roughly 80, to 16,000,

00:03:02.828 --> 00:03:04.830
well then you wouldn't have to multiply

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.960
by something that's close to 20,

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:06.930
you'd have to multiply by something

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.610
that's close to 200.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.163
So I like our answer.

